      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=2\\cdot {3}^{x}$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n                    \n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}{|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
